WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
LUNARIS: what if your lunar landing is late?
Choose a surface mission. See what a delay changes.

00:03.000 --> 00:10.000
Original arrival: 1 Nov, 06:00 UTC. PASS.
At least 7 h 53 min 52 s with Sun + Earth.

00:10.000 --> 00:13.500
Apply a 72-hour delay. Watch the shared UTC clock.
This is a time jump, not a spacecraft landing simulation.

00:13.500 --> 00:17.000
Delayed arrival: 4 Nov, 06:00 UTC. FAIL.
No qualified sunlight for 12 hours. Limit: 7 hours. Five hours too long.

00:17.000 --> 00:20.500
Find the next confirmed window. Keep all four limits.
Same study point, same 12-hour mission, hourly search grid.

00:20.500 --> 00:25.000
17 Nov, 03:00 UTC. PASS. Twelve hours with Sun + Earth.
Wait after delayed arrival: 12 days 21 hours. Reachability is not modeled.

00:25.000 --> 00:29.000
Seven separate tested cases pass. Combined uncertainties were not evaluated.
NASA LOLA terrain, JPL ephemerides and Horizons checks: geometry, not power or radio.
